{"key":"apphy2-mcq-004","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"A","final_answer":"a positive test charge","working":"By definition, the electric field vector E at a given point in space is defined as the electrostatic force F experienced by a small positive test charge q placed at that point, divided by the magnitude of that charge: E = F / q (where q > 0). Consequently, the direction of the electric field is identical to the direction of the force exerted on a positive test charge.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":347,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":347,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":244,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":115,"reasoningTokens":129},"totalTokens":591,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":129,"promptTokenCount":347,"candidatesTokenCount":115,"totalTokenCount":591,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":347}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":115}]},"reasoningTokens":129,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":3432,"keyed_label":"A"}
